    "progress": "Ryan probed two design points, answered in session: (1) 10GB cap => keep DO size O(live work): event retention window (full history in Iceberg), closed tickets become ~200B stubs w/ R2 pointer, self-monitoring via databaseSize + alarms, facets/split-shard as last resorts. (2) Cross-DO queries => never scatter-gather (6 concurrent outbound conns/Worker); all cross-project reads served by derived stores fed from the event stream: D1 directory of LIVE tickets (my-work, global ready, ref routing), AI Search/Vectorize for global search, Iceberg+R2 SQL for history. Cross-project edges via idempotent event delivery (event ULIDs as dedupe keys); cross-project cascade eventually consistent (~seconds). VERIFY LATER: DO Facets per-facet storage caps."
